-`provenance.md` (in an issue's or a raft's folder) is the one record of what git cannot tell: a header, the table header and one row per event, `| when | event | actor | detail |`, no row numbers, appended and never edited (`./zn audit` checks it; the file is exactly that grammar and a stray line is an error). The events are `approved`, `unblocked`, `confirmed`, `ranked`, `rafted` and `delivered`. `./zn record <id> unblocked|confirmed|ranked [--actor A] [--detail k=v]` publishes `unblocked`, `confirmed` and `ranked` for a backlog issue or raft (the tickets that make those events call it), `unblocked` only for an active one and nothing for a done one; the other events are written by their own commands in a pull request. The **actor** is `human:<git name>` or `agent:<model> effort <level>`: `--actor`, else `ZN_ACTOR` (the dispatcher sets it), else `agent:unknown effort <CLAUDE_EFFORT>` when `CLAUDECODE`, `AI_AGENT`, `CURSOR_AGENT` (the `agent` CLI), `GROK_SESSION_ID` (the `grok` CLI) or `ZN_DISPATCH` (a dispatched step) is set and non-empty, else the git name. A published append is built from `origin/main`'s file. **Merging.** Two writers (a published row on `main`, a row in your PR) are united by the engine's own merges of `origin/main`: merge with `./zn sync` (the commands that merge for you do the same: `land`, `fold`, `recombine`, `new raft` and every command that publishes, which merges `origin/main` afterwards), and let it unite the record, wherever the item's folder moved and however git paired the files: it settles every record either side changed, by the item's id, and puts it beside the item's document. It stops, with nothing left half merged, for a conflict in another file, a record that does not parse, a record both sides changed where a side edited, removed or reordered an old row, an item whose id changed on one side (a `renumber`, or a compaction: run `./zn remap`), a merge that crosses a compaction (a side numbers items differently from the merge base) when a record changed on the other side (run `./zn remap`; on the compaction's own branch, compact again on the current `origin/main`), and an uncommitted change to a record it would have to rewrite (commit or stash it); and it refuses while a merge of a branch `origin/main` does not contain, a cherry-pick, a revert or a rebase is in progress. When it stops on another file, merge by hand: `git merge origin/main`, resolve every conflict except `provenance.md`, `git add` the files, and run `./zn sync` again: it finishes that merge (a merge of `origin/main` or of an older commit of it), merges the newest `origin/main` on top, and unites the records (`origin/main`'s new rows first, then yours, every old row as it was). After a `renumber`, merge that item's record by hand under its new id. `remap` settles the records the same way; when it stops, merge by hand: its merge base is from before the compaction, so `./zn sync` would stop on the compaction, and `remap` refuses a second run.
